IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `wra-core`
IMPORT `wra-definitions`

-- wra3-sch9.l4: the Welfare Reform Act 2012 (United Kingdom), 2012 c. 5, Schedule 9 (personal independence payment:
-- amendments). Part wra3, layer 1. Written from inputs/ukpga-2012-5.txt, a plain-text rendering of legislation.gov.uk
-- (version 2026-07-01), not the official text.
--
-- Host Acts (not among the sources): SSCBA = Social Security Contributions and Benefits Act 1992; SSAA = Social Security
-- Administration Act 1992; SSA1998 = Social Security Act 1998; SSFA = Social Security Fraud Act 2001.
-- The paragraph numbers of Schedule 9 are not printed in the text. They are counted by cross-heading and by the
-- "is amended as follows" lines (Transport Act 1982 para 1; Child Support Act 1991 para 2; SSCBA paras 3 to 6; SSAA paras
-- 7 to 33; Recovery of Benefits Act 1997 paras 34 to 36; SSA1998 paras 37 to 43; Immigration and Asylum Act 1999 para 44;
-- SSFA paras 45 to 47; ITEPA 2003 paras 48 to 50): DERIVED and uncorroborated.
--
-- Most of Schedule 9 adds "personal independence payment" to a list or a cross-reference in another Act whose own text is
-- not among the sources. Those amendments are inert (reason 2: amendments of other Acts): the inserted words state no rule
-- of their own, and what they mean to the individual depends on the host provision's lead-in, which is not printed here.
-- Six units are encoded: SSCBA 64(1A), SSAA 73(6), SSA1998 Sch 3 para 3(h) and (i), the two SSFA 6A(1)(ca) limbs (the third
-- limb of seam 7 of PLAN.md, see NOTES.md), the SSFA 10(3)(be) limb, which has the same words as the disqualifying-benefit
-- limb, and the SSAA 187(1)(ad) limb. The last four are free-standing paragraphs of a list that another part's Schedule also
-- adds a paragraph to, so the lead needs each as a function to compose the list at the merge (assumed, not ruled).

§ `sch 9 SSCBA 64(1A) allowances within the subsection`

-- SSCBA 64(1A): The following allowances are within this subsection: (a) personal independence payment; (b) the care
-- component of a disability living allowance. The text lists two and does not close the list.
-- src:3250 | (1A) The following allowances are within this subsection—
-- src:3251 | (a) personal independence payment;
-- src:3252 | (b) the care component of a disability living allowance.
@ref sch 9 para 5 SSCBA 64(1A) (src:3250-3252)
DECLARE `sch 9 para 5 allowance` IS ONE OF
    `sch 9 para 5 SSCBA 64(1A)(a) personal independence payment`
    `sch 9 para 5 SSCBA 64(1A)(b) the care component of a disability living allowance`
    `sch 9 para 5 any other allowance`

@ref sch 9 para 5 SSCBA 64(1A) (src:3250-3252)
GIVEN `the allowance` IS A `sch 9 para 5 allowance`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`sch 9 para 5 SSCBA 64(1A) the allowance is within subsection (1A)` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the allowance`
    WHEN `sch 9 para 5 SSCBA 64(1A)(a) personal independence payment` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `sch 9 para 5 SSCBA 64(1A)(b) the care component of a disability living allowance` THEN JUST TRUE
    -- NOTHING-kind (list not closed): "The following allowances are within this subsection" does not say that no other allowance is
    WHEN `sch 9 para 5 any other allowance` THEN NOTHING

§ `sch 9 SSAA 73(6) overlapping benefits`

-- SSAA 73(6): Personal independence payment is to be treated for the purposes of this section as if it were benefit as
-- defined in section 122 of the Contributions and Benefits Act.
-- src:3269 | (6) Personal independence payment is to be treated for the purposes of this section as if it were benefit as defined in section 122 of the Contributions and Benefits Act.
@ref sch 9 para 11 SSAA 73(6) (src:3269)
GIVEN `the benefit` IS A Benefit
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`sch 9 para 11 SSAA 73(6) the benefit is treated for the purposes of section 73 as if it were benefit as defined in section 122 of the Contributions and Benefits Act` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the benefit`
    WHEN `personal independence payment` THEN JUST TRUE
    -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the deeming is for "Personal independence payment"; the subsection is silent on any other benefit
    OTHERWISE NOTHING

§ `sch 9 SSAA 187(1) inalienability`

-- SSAA 187(1): in section 187 (inalienability), in subsection (1), after paragraph (ac) there is inserted (ad) personal
-- independence payment. The text prints the section's title, "inalienability", and does not print the lead-in of subsection (1).
-- Schedule 2 of this Act (raw line 2794, another part's range) inserts (za) universal credit before paragraph (a) of the same
-- subsection, so this is ONE limb of a list that the lead composes at the merge (see NOTES.md, Seams).
-- src:3306 | In section 187 (inalienability), in subsection (1), after paragraph (ac) there is inserted—
-- src:3307 | (ad) personal independence payment;
@ref sch 9 para 31 SSAA 187(1)(ad) (src:3306-3307)
GIVEN `the benefit` IS A Benefit
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`sch 9 para 31 SSAA 187(1)(ad) the benefit is within the limb` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the benefit`
    WHEN `personal independence payment` THEN JUST TRUE
    -- NOTHING-kind (list not closed): the amendment adds one paragraph to a list whose other paragraphs are in the host Act or in another part's range
    OTHERWISE NOTHING

§ `sch 9 SSA1998 Sch 3 para 3 decisions against which an appeal lies`

-- SSA1998 Sch 3 para 3: after paragraph (g) there are inserted (h) regulations made under section 85(1) or 86(1) of the
-- Welfare Reform Act 2012; (i) section 87 of that Act. The text prints the Schedule's title as "decisions against which an
-- appeal lies" (raw line 3335) and does not print the lead-in of paragraph 3 of that Schedule: see fork F-sch9-1.
-- src:3335 | In Schedule 3 (decisions against which an appeal lies), in paragraph 3—
-- src:3336 | (a) in paragraph (f), the final “or” is repealed;
-- src:3337 | (b) after paragraph (g) there is inserted—
-- src:3338 | (h) regulations made under section 85(1) or 86(1) of the Welfare Reform Act 2012;
-- src:3339 | (i) section 87 of that Act.
@ref sch 9 para 43 SSA1998 Sch 3 para 3(h)-(i) (src:3335-3339)
DECLARE `sch 9 para 43 decision` IS ONE OF
    `sch 9 para 43 SSA1998 Sch 3 para 3(h) a decision as to regulations made under section 85(1) or 86(1) of the Welfare Reform Act 2012`
    `sch 9 para 43 SSA1998 Sch 3 para 3(i) a decision as to section 87 of the Welfare Reform Act 2012`
    `sch 9 para 43 any other decision`

@ref sch 9 para 43 SSA1998 Sch 3 para 3(h)-(i) (src:3335-3339)
GIVEN `the decision` IS A `sch 9 para 43 decision`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`sch 9 para 43 SSA1998 Sch 3 para 3(h) and (i) an appeal lies against the decision` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the decision`
    -- the Schedule is entitled "decisions against which an appeal lies" (line 3335) and paragraph (h) names these decisions (a lawyer's reading: F-sch9-1)
    WHEN `sch 9 para 43 SSA1998 Sch 3 para 3(h) a decision as to regulations made under section 85(1) or 86(1) of the Welfare Reform Act 2012` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `sch 9 para 43 SSA1998 Sch 3 para 3(i) a decision as to section 87 of the Welfare Reform Act 2012` THEN JUST TRUE
    -- NOTHING-kind (list not closed): the text inserts two paragraphs into a list whose other paragraphs are not among the sources
    WHEN `sch 9 para 43 any other decision` THEN NOTHING

§ `sch 9 SSFA 6A(1) disqualifying and sanctionable benefit`

-- SSFA 6A(1): in the definition of "disqualifying benefit", after paragraph (c) there is inserted (ca) any benefit under
-- Part 4 of the Welfare Reform Act 2012 (personal independence payment) or under any provision in Northern Ireland which
-- corresponds to that Part; in the definition of "sanctionable benefit", after paragraph (c) there is inserted (ca)
-- personal independence payment. Each is ONE limb of a list in the host Act, and the other limbs are not among these
-- sources or belong to other parts (seam 7 of PLAN.md), so each answers NOTHING for a benefit its limb does not name.
-- src:3346 | In section 6A(1) (definitions)—
-- src:3347 | (a) in the definition of “disqualifying benefit”, after paragraph (c) there is inserted—
-- src:3348 | (ca) any benefit under Part 4 of the Welfare Reform Act 2012 (personal independence payment) or under any provision in Northern Ireland which corresponds to that Part;
-- src:3349 | (b) in the definition of “sanctionable benefit”, after paragraph (c) there is inserted—
-- src:3350 | (ca) personal independence payment;
@ref sch 9 para 46 SSFA 6A(1) (src:3346-3350)
GIVEN `the benefit` IS A Benefit
      `the benefit is under a provision in Northern Ireland which corresponds to Part 4 of the Welfare Reform Act 2012` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`sch 9 para 46 SSFA 6A(1) disqualifying benefit (ca) the benefit is within the limb` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `the benefit` EQUALS `personal independence payment` THEN JUST TRUE
        IF `the benefit is under a provision in Northern Ireland which corresponds to Part 4 of the Welfare Reform Act 2012` THEN JUST TRUE
        -- NOTHING-kind (list not closed): limb (ca) names benefits under Part 4 (or the Northern Ireland equivalent) only; the other limbs of "disqualifying benefit" are in the host Act and in other parts
        OTHERWISE NOTHING

@ref sch 9 para 46 SSFA 6A(1) (src:3349-3350)
GIVEN `the benefit` IS A Benefit
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`sch 9 para 46 SSFA 6A(1) sanctionable benefit (ca) the benefit is within the limb` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `the benefit` EQUALS `personal independence payment` THEN JUST TRUE
        -- NOTHING-kind (list not closed): limb (ca) names personal independence payment only; the other limbs of "sanctionable benefit" are in the host Act and in other parts
        OTHERWISE NOTHING

§ `sch 9 SSFA 10(3) benefit within the power to supplement and mitigate loss of benefit provisions`

-- SSFA 10(3): after paragraph (bd) there is inserted (be) any benefit under Part 4 of the Welfare Reform Act 2012 (personal
-- independence payment) or under any provision in Northern Ireland which corresponds to that Part. It is one limb of a list in
-- the host Act (the benefits whose loss-of-benefit provisions the power in section 10 may supplement or mitigate), and the
-- other limbs are not among these sources, so it answers NOTHING for a benefit its limb does not name.
-- src:3351 | In section 10 (power to supplement and mitigate loss of benefit provisions), in subsection (3), after paragraph (bd) (inserted by Schedule 2 to this Act) there is inserted—
-- src:3352 | (be) any benefit under Part 4 of the Welfare Reform Act 2012 (personal independence payment) or under any provision in Northern Ireland which corresponds to that Part;
@ref sch 9 para 47 SSFA 10(3)(be) (src:3351-3352)
GIVEN `the benefit` IS A Benefit
      `the benefit is under a provision in Northern Ireland which corresponds to Part 4 of the Welfare Reform Act 2012` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`sch 9 para 47 SSFA 10(3)(be) the benefit is within the limb` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `the benefit` EQUALS `personal independence payment` THEN JUST TRUE
        IF `the benefit is under a provision in Northern Ireland which corresponds to Part 4 of the Welfare Reform Act 2012` THEN JUST TRUE
        -- NOTHING-kind (list not closed): limb (be) names benefits under Part 4 (or the Northern Ireland equivalent) only; the other limbs of section 10(3) are in the host Act
        OTHERWISE NOTHING
